Package: apklayer
Architecture: arm64 amd64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, ${apklayer:Depends},
 openjdk-21-jre-headless, python3, python3-gi, zip, unzip, wget, zstd, uidmap
Recommends: mesa-utils, pkexec, xdg-utils, desktop-file-utils,
 gstreamer1.0-plugins-good, gstreamer1.0-plugins-bad, gstreamer1.0-libav
Suggests: ${apklayer:Suggests}
Description: run Android apps on Linux in Wayland windows
 apklayer runs Android apps (APKs) as Linux processes: the app's dex code is
 converted to JVM classes once, Android's own native libraries run through
 bionic_translation, and each app opens a Wayland window. This package holds
 the command line tool, the window shell, the native runtime and
 apklayer-manager; the Android runtime bundle (Android's libraries and
 framework) is downloaded per user by apklayer-manager.

Package: apklayer-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
Depends: apklayer (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: apklayer hardware plugin API (headers and pkg-config file)
 Headers and apklayer-plugin.pc for building apklayer hardware plugins out of
 tree: sensors, GNSS, vibrator and camera backends, libraries
 libapklayer-<domain>-<backend>.so installed into the pkg-config variable
 plugindir (/usr/lib/<multiarch>/apklayer/plugins), where apklayer finds
 them. Guide: docs/PLUGINS.md in the apklayer sources.
